{"id": "000VJ7", "title": "Boulder Roll", "posted": "Heute, 16:00 Uhr", "author": "Artham", "rules": "I wanted to call this one Indiana Jones, but there might be copyright issues ;)\n\nClick here to solve on Sudokupad\n\nFill the grid with digits from 1 to 9 so that no digit repeats in a region. Digits might repeat in a row or column.\n\nBoulder Roll: Each boulder will enter the grid and roll in a straight line along its row or column until it exits the opposite side of the grid. As it rolls, it imprints a repeating sequence of digits onto the cells it passes through. The boulder's size determines how many cells it must traverse to complete one roll.\n\nFor example, a size-4 boulder entering from the left edge of a row might imprint the sequence 1-3-4-8-1-3-4-8-1 in the row.\n\nThermo Boulders: In this puzzle, boulders behave like thermometers: the boulder's one-roll pattern must be strictly increasing in the direction of travel. A boulder may have already started rolling before it entered the grid, so the first digit it imprints doesn't have to be the first digit of its pattern.\n\nConsecutive Kropki: If two digits are separated by a locust, they are consecutive.\n\nRatio Kropki: If two digits are separated by a scarab, one is double the other.\n\nMaximum cells: A digit on a diamond is greater than each of its four orthogonal neighbours.", "solutionCode": "Row 5 from left to right", "difficulty": 2, "solvedCount": 3, "tags": ["Sudoku"], "links": [{"url": "https://sudokupad.app/malum8h6kd", "kind": "sudokupad"}], "firstSeen": "2026-10-17T17:00:00+00:00", "data": "", "link": "https://sudokupad.app/malum8h6kd", "linkKind": "sudokupad", "settings": {}, "summary": {"format": "scl", "decoded": true, "rows": 9, "cols": 9, "cages": 0, "hasSolution": true, "features": ["overlays", "underlays"]}}